{"ts":"2026-10-23T09:09:56.530226068Z","session":"837b52b4-d41d-4919-9e09-c68083ddd2a3","tool":"Agent","tool_input":{"description":"Fix spec review findings","prompt":"Local-review fix on PR #536 (bead ethos-5y4r). Repo \u003crepo\u003e, branch design/opencode-plugin-adapter, checked out — do not create or switch branches. Commit on this branch; do not push, do not touch PRs or threads, do not merge — the leader does that. Write set: docs/spec-opencode-lifecycle.tex only; commit by explicit path. `make check` must pass (read full output) before each commit. Harness .tmp/lc3/ (exp3.sh etc). If a fix proves impossible, stop and report.\n\nFix all of these (leader decisions):\n1. Add a limit (N22): LcCfRefuse over-approximates the design's read phase. It needs only c? not in dom stage, so the model reaches a refusal while the child holds a claim. In the design, read-phase step 2 reads the child's claim first and takes the claimed case. Through the real entry point, a refusal with a claim needs the claim to be written between the step-2 lock-free read and the dispatch-pending lock. The refusal-path rows (C9_lfa_off, C17_off_noop, MutClaimLiveRefuse) model that interleaving.\n2. LiveSpared and ReconcileOnExit prose (~428, ~449-451, ~457-459, ledger ~2283): restate both items in terms of the full liveness predicate (binding, complete mark, or, under fixClaimLive, an owned dkFork skeleton, each together with the claim). Say that the \"binding-or-complete\" wording describes the predicate with fixClaimLive off.\n3. ~2343-2345: the NoLiveForkAborted necessity claim cites C17_nodur, which checks NoOrphanOpenSkeleton. Either add and run a row with goal `liveForkAborted /= {}` and fixDurableName off (all others on), or move the fixDurableName clause to the NoOrphanOpenSkeleton sentence. Prefer the run; record it in the table.\n4. ~2532-2535: Reach_nosup is a not-durable isolating row with fixClaimLive on. Re-run it with fixClaimLive off so its stated trace stands, update the row, and include it in the rule's list.\n5. Mark the old liveness rule as withdrawn where it still stands. The C12 item of the design-consequences list (~3059-3062, \"an incomplete one keeps the rule of C4\") and ~2999-3000 (\"unless the binding is live\"): add the withdrawal note pointing to C17 / fixClaimLive, as the C12 ledger entry has.\n6. Ghost paragraph: liveForkAborted reads the claim, owner, kind, the skeleton's mission, and the open-to-aborted change. Make sure the spec text says so wherever it lists what the ghost reads.\nUpdate row counts everywhere if rows are added. Report commit hash(es), new or changed row figures, and any outcome change.","subagent_type":"jms"},"tool_input_hash":"14b1b902a31fd9cb0cb4d0e98270a155e449360faba4e326a965346c417f89af","tool_input_preview":"{\"description\":\"Fix spec review findings\",\"prompt\":\"Local-review fix on PR #536 (bead ethos-5y4r). Repo \\u003crepo\\u003e, branch design/opencode-plugin-adapter, checked out — do not create or switch..."}
